# ComposeIO Composer Intelligence API [SPEC:CXC-INTEL-API]

> The Composer's internal bus namespace registry IS the Intelligence command taxonomy. An Intelligence that can publish ComposeIO bus messages can design UX — placing widgets, wiring bindings, configuring properties — indistinguishable from human interaction. This spec formalizes the protocol for Intelligence participation.

---

## 1. Governing Principle [CXC-INTEL-PRINCIPLE]

> An Intelligence is a bus client. The Composer's visual canvas is a bus client. They are peers. Neither is privileged. The bus is the design engine; everything else is a view.

- implication: Every action achievable by clicking the canvas is achievable by publishing a bus message. There is no "visual-only" capability. The Intelligence API is not an adapter or wrapper — it is the same namespace registry that modules use.
- implication: An Intelligence can design a complete UX headlessly (no Composer window). The `.compose.yaml` is generated from bus state, not from canvas state. The canvas renders bus state — it does not own it.
- implication: Human and Intelligence can co-edit simultaneously. Both publish to the same namespaces. The History module records all commands regardless of source. Undo works uniformly.
- see-also: [DP-CXC-10] Intelligence-Friendly by Default.

---

## 2. Intelligence Lifecycle [CXC-INTEL-LIFECYCLE]

### [CXC-INTEL-JOIN] Joining the Bus

An Intelligence joins the Composer's internal bus by connecting as a transport client and announcing itself:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/joined
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "capabilities": ["layout", "binding", "property", "review"],
  "mode": "collaborative",
  "source": "claude-designer-1"
}
```

- `agent_id`: Unique identifier for this Intelligence session.
- `capabilities`: Declared capability set (what this agent can do).
- `mode`: `collaborative` (works alongside human), `autonomous` (drives design independently), `review` (read-only observation and suggestions).

### [CXC-INTEL-LEAVE] Leaving the Bus

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/left
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "source": "claude-designer-1"
}
```

### [CXC-INTEL-HEARTBEAT] Presence

While connected, the Intelligence publishes heartbeat every 10 seconds:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/heartbeat
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "active_task": "placing gauge widgets",
  "source": "claude-designer-1"
}
```

- The Toolbar module shows Intelligence presence (agent icon + active task description).
- If heartbeat is missed for 30 seconds, the Composer marks the Intelligence as disconnected.

---

## 3. Command Taxonomy [CXC-INTEL-COMMANDS]

The Intelligence uses the SAME namespaces defined in [SPEC:CXC-INTERNAL-BUS]. No separate API. The following is the complete command vocabulary organized by design workflow phase.

### 3.1 Structure Commands (Create/Delete)

| Action | Namespace | Event Data |
|---|---|---|
| Add module | `composer/canvas/module_added` | `{module_id, role, layout: {grid_row, grid_column, weight_x, weight_y, padding}, config: {columns, ...}}` |
| Remove module | `composer/canvas/module_removed` | `{module_id}` |
| Add widget | `composer/canvas/widget_added` | `{widget_id, widget_type, module_id, namespace, properties: {...}, layout: {row, column, rowspan, columnspan}}` |
| Remove widget | `composer/canvas/widget_removed` | `{widget_id}` |
| Add namespace | `composer/config/namespace_changed` | `{action: "created", name, label, state_engine, scope, authority}` |
| Remove namespace | `composer/config/namespace_changed` | `{action: "removed", name}` |

### 3.2 Layout Commands (Move/Resize)

| Action | Namespace | Event Data |
|---|---|---|
| Move widget | `composer/canvas/widget_moved` | `{widget_id, old_layout: {row, column}, new_layout: {row, column}}` |
| Resize widget | `composer/canvas/widget_resized` | `{widget_id, old_layout: {rowspan, columnspan}, new_layout: {rowspan, columnspan}}` |
| Change module layout | `composer/canvas/layout_changed` | `{module_id, layout: {grid_row, grid_column, weight_x, weight_y}}` |
| Rearrange design grid | `composer/canvas/layout_changed` | `{design_grid: {columns, rows, weights: [...]}}` |

### 3.3 Configuration Commands (Properties)

| Action | Namespace | Event Data |
|---|---|---|
| Change widget property | `composer/config/widget_changed` | `{widget_id, property, old_value, new_value}` |
| Change module property | `composer/config/module_changed` | `{module_id, property, old_value, new_value}` |
| Change namespace config | `composer/config/namespace_changed` | `{action: "modified", name, property, old_value, new_value}` |

### 3.4 Binding Commands

| Action | Namespace | Event Data |
|---|---|---|
| Create simple binding | `composer/binding/created` | `{binding_id, type: "simple", config: {input, output, transform: [...]}}` |
| Create compound binding | `composer/binding/created` | `{binding_id, type: "compound", config: {output, requires, default, conditions: [...]}}` |
| Create event binding | `composer/binding/created` | `{binding_id, type: "event_triggered", config: {trigger, output, set, side_effects: [...]}}` |
| Modify binding | `composer/binding/modified` | `{binding_id, config: {...}}` |
| Remove binding | `composer/binding/removed` | `{binding_id}` |

### 3.5 File Commands

| Action | Namespace | Event Data |
|---|---|---|
| Save design | `composer/file/saved` | `{path}` |
| Load design | `composer/file/loaded` | `{path}` (or `{yaml_content}` for inline) |
| Export to ComposeIO YAML | `composer/file/exported` | `{output_dir}` |

### 3.6 Selection Commands (for context awareness)

| Action | Namespace | Event Data |
|---|---|---|
| Select widget | `composer/selection/widget_id` | `widget_id` string value |
| Select module | `composer/selection/module_id` | `module_id` string value |
| Clear selection | `composer/selection/type` | `none` |

---

## 4. Message Sequencing [CXC-INTEL-SEQUENCING]

### [CXC-INTEL-SEQ-RULES] Ordering Constraints

Bus messages are asynchronous, but design operations have logical dependencies:

| Operation | Prerequisite |
|---|---|
| Add widget to module | Module must exist |
| Assign namespace to widget | Namespace must be registered |
| Create binding referencing namespace | Namespace must exist |
| Move widget within module | Widget must exist |
| Change widget property | Widget must exist |

The Intelligence MUST ensure prerequisites are met before publishing dependent commands. The Composer validates and rejects out-of-order commands with an error event:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/error
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "command": "composer/canvas/widget_added",
  "error": "module 'ftl_panel' does not exist",
  "suggestion": "publish composer/canvas/module_added first"
}
```

### [CXC-INTEL-SEQ-BATCH] Batch Operations

For atomic multi-step operations, the Intelligence uses batch IDs (same as [CXC-IBUS-CONV-4]):

```json
{"batch_id": "intel_batch_001", "batch_index": 0, "batch_total": 6, ...}
{"batch_id": "intel_batch_001", "batch_index": 1, "batch_total": 6, ...}
```

- The History module treats the batch as a single undoable unit.
- The Preview module waits for the complete batch before rebuilding (avoids intermediate states).
- Batch ordering is sequential by `batch_index`.

### [CXC-INTEL-SEQ-RECIPE] Common Recipes

#### Recipe: Create a complete module with widgets and bindings

```
1. PUBLISH composer/config/namespace_changed  {action: "created", name: "ftl_arm", ...}
2. PUBLISH composer/config/namespace_changed  {action: "created", name: "ftl_cap_charge", ...}
3. PUBLISH composer/canvas/module_added       {id: "ftl_panel", role: "button-matrix", ...}
4. PUBLISH composer/canvas/widget_added       {id: "btn_arm", module: "ftl_panel", namespace: "ftl_arm", ...}
5. PUBLISH composer/canvas/widget_added       {id: "btn_sub", module: "ftl_panel", namespace: "sublight_engines", ...}
6. PUBLISH composer/binding/created           {type: "compound", output: "ftl_jump_led", ...}
```

All 6 messages carry the same `batch_id`. Human sees the entire module appear atomically.

#### Recipe: Refactor layout (move widgets between modules)

```
1. PUBLISH composer/canvas/widget_removed     {widget_id: "gauge_cap"}         — remove from old module
2. PUBLISH composer/canvas/widget_added       {widget_id: "gauge_cap", module_id: "new_panel", ...}  — add to new
```

Batch of 2. Undo restores the widget to its original module.

---

## 5. Co-Editing Protocol [CXC-INTEL-COEDIT]

### [CXC-INTEL-COEDIT-PRINCIPLE] Conflict-Free Co-Editing

Human and Intelligence publish to the same bus. Conflicts arise when both modify the same object simultaneously.

### [CXC-INTEL-COEDIT-RULES] Conflict Resolution Rules

| Rule | Description |
|---|---|
| Last-write-wins for properties | If human and Intelligence both change the same widget property, the later message wins. History records both. |
| Human always wins on selection | If the human selects a widget, the Intelligence should not programmatically change selection. |
| Intelligence yields on drag | If a widget is being dragged (human interaction in progress), the Intelligence defers layout changes to that widget until drag completes. |
| Batch atomicity | An Intelligence batch in progress is completed before human actions on affected objects are processed. |

### [CXC-INTEL-COEDIT-AWARENESS] Mutual Awareness

The Intelligence subscribes to all `composer/` namespaces to observe human actions:

```
SUBSCRIBE composer/selection/*         — Know what the human is looking at
SUBSCRIBE composer/canvas/*            — Know what the human is building
SUBSCRIBE composer/config/*            — Know what the human is configuring
SUBSCRIBE composer/tool/mode           — Know the human's current interaction mode
SUBSCRIBE composer/connection/*        — Know the bus connection state
```

The human sees Intelligence activity via:
- Toolbar: Agent icon + active task from heartbeat
- Canvas: Widgets added by Intelligence have a subtle agent badge (removable)
- History: Commands show source (`source: "claude-designer-1"` vs `source: "canvas"`)

### [CXC-INTEL-COEDIT-INTENT] Intent Declaration

Before performing a large operation, the Intelligence SHOULD declare intent:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/intent
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "action": "Creating FTL jump control panel with 5 buttons, 2 gauges, and compound bindings",
  "affected_modules": ["ftl_panel", "gauge_panel"],
  "estimated_commands": 15,
  "source": "claude-designer-1"
}
```

The Composer MAY display this to the human as a toast notification. The human can preemptively cancel by publishing:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/cancel
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "reason": "I want to do this differently"
}
```

The Intelligence subscribes to `composer/intelligence/cancel` and aborts.

---

## 6. Observation API [CXC-INTEL-OBSERVE]

### [CXC-INTEL-OBSERVE-STATE] Reading Current Design State

The Intelligence can request a full design state snapshot:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/request_state
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1"
}
```

The Composer responds:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/state_snapshot
{
  "design": { ... full DesignDocument as JSON ... },
  "namespaces": [ ... current namespace values from design bus ... ],
  "connection_status": "connected",
  "selection": { "type": "widget", "widget_id": "btn_arm" }
}
```

### [CXC-INTEL-OBSERVE-DESIGNBUS] Observing the Design Bus

The Intelligence can subscribe to the design bus to observe hardware state, namespace values, and message flow. This enables reactive design:

| Observation | Response |
|---|---|
| New module discovered on design bus | Intelligence auto-generates widget panel matching module's role and namespaces |
| Namespace value out of expected range | Intelligence suggests binding or transform adjustment |
| Binding not firing as expected | Intelligence diagnoses condition mismatch, suggests fix |

### [CXC-INTEL-OBSERVE-LAYOUT] Spatial Understanding


```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/request_layout
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1",
  "target": "preview"          — or "canvas"
}
```

Response includes `report_layout_flat()` output: widget bounds, overlap detection, reading order — giving the Intelligence pixel-accurate spatial understanding of the current design.

---

## 7. Headless Mode [CXC-INTEL-HEADLESS]

### [CXC-INTEL-HEADLESS-PRINCIPLE] No Window Required

The Composer can run without a visual window. In headless mode:
- The internal bus exists and processes all messages.
- The `DesignDocument` state model is maintained.
- The Canvas, Preview, and other visual modules are not instantiated.
- File save/load and export work normally.
- The Intelligence drives design entirely via bus messages.

```python
from composer.app import ComposerApp

app = ComposerApp(headless=True)
bus = app.internal_bus

# Intelligence publishes commands...
bus.publish_event("composer/canvas/module_added", "create", data={...})
bus.publish_event("composer/canvas/widget_added", "create", data={...})

# Save result
bus.publish_event("composer/file/saved", "save", data={"path": "my_design.compose.yaml"})
```

- use-case: CI/CD pipelines generating UX configs from specifications.
- use-case: Intelligence generating designs in batch without GUI overhead.
- use-case: Testing — validate that a sequence of bus commands produces the expected `.compose.yaml`.

### [CXC-INTEL-HEADLESS-VALIDATION] Headless Validation

In headless mode, the Intelligence can request validation:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/validate
{
  "agent_id": "claude-designer-1"
}
```

Response:

```
PUBLISH composer/intelligence/validation_result
{
  "valid": false,
  "errors": [
    {"type": "namespace_no_publisher", "namespace": "ftl_cap_charge"},
    {"type": "binding_missing_namespace", "binding": "bind_003", "namespace": "ftl_coord_status"}
  ],
  "warnings": [
    {"type": "namespace_no_subscriber", "namespace": "gauge_power"}
  ]
}
```

---

## 8. Intelligence Namespace Domain [CXC-INTEL-NAMESPACES]

All Intelligence-specific namespaces live under the `composer/intelligence/` prefix:

| Namespace | Type | Publisher | Subscriber | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/intelligence/joined` | event | Intelligence | Toolbar, Canvas | Agent connected |
| `composer/intelligence/left` | event | Intelligence | Toolbar, Canvas | Agent disconnected |
| `composer/intelligence/heartbeat` | state | Intelligence | Toolbar | Presence + active task |
| `composer/intelligence/intent` | event | Intelligence | Toolbar (toast) | Declares upcoming operation |
| `composer/intelligence/cancel` | event | Human (Toolbar) | Intelligence | Cancel current operation |
| `composer/intelligence/error` | event | Composer | Intelligence | Command rejected with reason |
| `composer/intelligence/request_state` | event | Intelligence | DesignDocument | Request full state snapshot |
| `composer/intelligence/state_snapshot` | event | DesignDocument | Intelligence | Full state response |
| `composer/intelligence/request_layout` | event | Intelligence | Preview/Canvas | Request spatial layout |
| `composer/intelligence/layout_snapshot` | event | Preview/Canvas | Intelligence | Layout response |
| `composer/intelligence/validate` | event | Intelligence | Serialization | Request design validation |
| `composer/intelligence/validation_result` | event | Serialization | Intelligence | Validation result |
| `composer/intelligence/suggestion` | event | Intelligence | Toolbar (notification) | Non-imperative suggestion to human |

---

## 9. Design Bus Intelligence Integration [CXC-INTEL-DESIGNBUS]

The Intelligence participates in the design bus as well as the internal bus. This enables:

### [CXC-INTEL-DESIGNBUS-DISCOVERY] Auto-Discovery Response

When a hardware module publishes `discovery` on the design bus, the Intelligence can automatically generate a matching Composer module:

```
1. OBSERVE: design_bus discovery message from "ftl-panel" with role "button-matrix",
   namespaces ["ftl_arm", "sublight_engines", "rcs_thrusters"]
2. PUBLISH: composer/intelligence/intent {action: "Auto-generating panel for discovered ftl-panel"}
3. PUBLISH: composer/config/namespace_changed × 3 (register discovered namespaces)
4. PUBLISH: composer/canvas/module_added (create module matching role)
5. PUBLISH: composer/canvas/widget_added × 3 (one per namespace)
```

### [CXC-INTEL-DESIGNBUS-ASSET] Asset-Driven Design

The Intelligence can query the document store and bus storage to incorporate assets:

```
1. GET /api/v1/assets/ → list available images
2. GET /api/v1/collections/ui_themes → query theme definitions
3. PUBLISH composer/config/widget_changed {widget_id: "btn_arm", property: "image", new_value: "assets/scifi/arm_button.png"}
4. PUBLISH composer/config/widget_changed {widget_id: "btn_arm", property: "led_color_on", new_value: "#00FF88"}
```

The Intelligence assembles visual identity from stored assets — the sci-fi button example.

---

## 10. Security Boundaries [CXC-INTEL-SECURITY]

| Rule | Rationale |
|---|---|
| Intelligence cannot modify the Composer's own module layout | Internal tool layout is not the design; it's the tool. |
| Intelligence MUST use `source: "<agent_id>"` on all messages | Auditability. History tracks who did what. |
| Intelligence cannot suppress undo recording | Every command is recorded. The human can always revert. |
| Intelligence cannot publish to design bus `_bus/` namespaces | Infrastructure namespaces are reserved for bus master. |
| Intelligence operating in `review` mode can only publish to `composer/intelligence/suggestion` | Read-only agents observe but do not modify. |

